# Description

camlf is a prototype for the [MLF] type system. It was first
developped by Didier Rémy, then extended with various features by
Gabriel Scherer, during his internship in the INRIA Gallium
team. Paolo Herms (a former INRIA internet) also contributed a first
version of explicit polymorphism.

 [MLF] http://pauillac.inria.fr/~remy/mlf/

The MLF type and inference engine used correspond to the gMLF type
system developped in Boris Yakobowski's [PhD thesis]. Compared to
Boris's prototype, the present one added an implementation of the
elaboration of xMLF terms from a solved graph.

 [PhD thesis] http://hal.inria.fr/tel-00357708/

This elaboration step, combined with a (new) implementation of the
xMLF language, is the final step of a complete toolchain for MLF
terms :
- parsing
- translation to gMLF constraints
- typing (resolution of the graphical constraints)
- translation of the solved graph into a xMLF term
- evaluation by reduction of the xMLF term

The main additional features to the gMLF type system are :
- explicit polymorphism according to (a variant of) Paolo Herms proposal (see [Paolo's report])
- a prototype (and yet experimental) implementation of the
  higher-order (Fω) features

A more complete description of the theoretical aspects and rationale
of the new developments can be found in [Gabriel's report].

 [Paolo's report] http://gallium.inria.fr/~remy/mlf/herms@master2009.pdf
 [Gabriel's report] yet to appear


# Examples

Some examples of MLF and explicit polymorphism can be found in the
Examples/ directory.

- `simple.mlf` : various MLF toy examples

- `church_encodings.mlf` : church encodings of boolean and integers

- `explicit.mlf` : toy examples of explicit polymorphism and its
  interaction with the implicit MLF inference

- `error.mlf` : demonstration of some ill-typed terms

- `recursion.mlf` : typing and xMLF reduction of recursive functions

# Dependencies

Dependencies :
- ocaml >= 3.11
- ocamlfind
- camomile (used for UTF-8 pretty-printing)

The pretty-printer also depends on Francois Pottier's Pprint library,
but the source code, patched for better UTF-8 support, is included in
the archive (pprint/ directory).

Optional dependencies :
- kaputt : required to build tests (gTest.ml / xTest.ml)
  http://kaputt.x9c.fr/
- lablgtk and odot : required to build the step-by-step graphical interface
  (interact.ml). It also depends on the 'odot' library, that can be installed standalone (

# Compilation

The provide Makefile has all the necessary build target

   # camlf, the main entry point (files, toplevel..)
   make camlf 
   
   # compile and run the GTK interactive reducer
   make interact 

   make clean


# Usage

Run `camlf` on files (`./camlf foo.mlf`) or as an
interactive toplevel (`./camlf -t`).

Usage :

  ./camlf <options> <files>

General options :

  --toplevel            toplevel : Read Eval Print Loop
  -t                    short for --toplevel

  --xmlf                activate the xmlf translation
  -x                   short for --xmlf

  --xmlf_reduce         activate evaluation by reduction of translated
                        xMLF terms

  -                     Read expression from stdin

  -expr <EXPR>	Typecheck expression <EXPR>


Result printing options :

  --constraint            show constraint
  --print_source          print source term.
  --print_desugared       print desugared source term.
  --dot Generate some dot files during typing.

  --xmlf_reduce_verbose   print intermediary reduction steps during xmlf
                          reduction (see 'xmlf_reduce' flag)

  --no-xmlf_utf8          disable UTF8 printing of xMLF terms and type

Predefined examples (examples.ml) :

  -use <NAME>	   typecheck predefined expression registered as <NAME>
  -all 	           typecheck all filtered predefined expressions
  -list 	   list predefined expression
  -filter <STRING> filter predefined definitions whose name matches <STRING>

Debugging options (for development purposes) :
  --backtrace          print backtraces for all exceptions.
  --xmlf_backtrace     print xmlf translation backtraces.
  --gmlf_bactrace      print gMLF translation backtraces.
